(function(E){ const x = E["exam-09"] = E["exam-09"] || {units:{}}; (x.units = x.units || {})["x09-r1"] = {"id":"x09-r1","patterns":["RA-tech","GT1-notices","GT1-reviews","PARA-research","PARA-rules","TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge","TR-paraphrase","TR-limit","TR-plural","TR-samewords","TR-detail"],"title":{"en":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","tr":"Reading 1: Passage 1 / Section 1","fa":"Reading ۱: متن ۱ (Passage 1) / بخش ۱ (Section 1)"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a history of a product, and then complete notes on its most recent stage with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir ürünün tarihiyle ilgili TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi, sonra en yeni aşamasıyla ilgili notları metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی تاریخچه‌ی یک کالا بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و بعد یادداشت‌های جدیدترین مرحله‌اش را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"objectiveGT":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a page of questions and answers, and to match statements to short reviews.","tr":"Bu derste bir soru-cevap sayfasında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi ve ifadeleri kısa yorumlarla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی یک صفحه‌ی پرسش و پاسخ بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و جمله‌ها را با نظرهای کوتاه جور کنی."},"sessions":[["explain"],["drill"],["exit"]],"explain":{"title":{"en":"Reading Passage 1: the history of a product","tr":"Reading Passage 1: bir ürünün tarihi","fa":"Reading Passage 1: تاریخچه‌ی یک کالا"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a history of a product, and then complete notes on its most recent stage with one word from the passage.","tr":"Bu derste bir ürünün tarihiyle ilgili TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi, sonra en yeni aşamasıyla ilgili notları metinden tek kelimeyle tamamlamayı öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی تاریخچه‌ی یک کالا بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و بعد یادداشت‌های جدیدترین مرحله‌اش را با یک کلمه از متن کامل کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"13"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"20 min","tr":"20 dk","fa":"۲۰ دقیقه"}},{"label":{"en":"Words","tr":"Kelime","fa":"کلمه"},"value":"~770"}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: running shoes","tr":"Bu sınav: koşu ayakkabıları","fa":"این آزمون: کفش دو"},"intro":{"en":"Passage 1 is usually a clear account in time order. Technology and design topics often follow one invention from its first form to today. The statements test small details, so read closely.","tr":"Passage 1 genelde zaman sırasına göre açık bir anlatımdır. Teknoloji ve tasarım konuları çoğu zaman bir icadı ilk biçiminden bugüne kadar izler. İfadeler küçük ayrıntıları ölçer; dikkatle oku.","fa":"Passage 1 معمولاً روایتی روشن به ترتیب زمان است. موضوع‌های فناوری و طراحی اغلب یک اختراع را از شکل اولش تا امروز دنبال می‌کنند. جمله‌ها جزئیات کوچک را می‌سنجند، پس با دقت بخوان."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x09-r1-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","PARA-research"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"How an everyday product has changed","tr":"Gündelik bir ürün nasıl değişti","fa":"یک کالای روزمره چطور تغییر کرد"},"asks":{"en":"A history of one product, decade by decade: early versions, a sudden change in demand, new technology, what research says about it, a backlash, the latest design and its problems. TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN comes first; the notes cover the most recent part.","tr":"Bir ürünün on yıl on yıl tarihi: ilk sürümler, talepte ani bir değişim, yeni teknoloji, araştırmaların ne dediği, bir tepki, en yeni tasarım ve sorunları. Önce TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN geliyor; notlar en yeni kısmı kapsıyor.","fa":"تاریخچه‌ی یک کالا، دهه به دهه: نسخه‌های اولیه، تغییری ناگهانی در تقاضا، فناوری تازه، آنچه پژوهش‌ها می‌گویند، یک واکنش مخالف، جدیدترین طراحی و مشکلاتش. اول TRUE/FALSE/NOT GIVEN می‌آید؛ یادداشت‌ها جدیدترین بخش را پوشش می‌دهند."},"fields":["The first versions","What changed and why","New technology","What research found","A new trend","Latest design","Problems for the future"],"words":[{"a":"cheap","b":"cost so little / inexpensive","tr":"ucuz","fa":"ارزان"},{"a":"a new market","b":"millions of new customers","tr":"yeni bir pazar","fa":"بازاری تازه"},{"a":"cushioning","b":"soft, thick soles / softens the impact","tr":"yastıklama","fa":"بالشتک، نرمی کف"},{"a":"introduced","b":"brought in / launched","tr":"piyasaya sürdü","fa":"معرفی کرد"},{"a":"little evidence","b":"research has not supported / no clear proof","tr":"az kanıt","fa":"شواهد کم"},{"a":"reduce injuries","b":"fewer injuries / protect runners","tr":"sakatlığı azaltmak","fa":"کم کردن آسیب"},{"a":"a trend faded","b":"became less popular / died out","tr":"bir eğilim söndü","fa":"یک روند از رونق افتاد"},{"a":"switched too quickly","b":"changed too fast","tr":"çok hızlı geçti","fa":"خیلی سریع عوض کرد"},{"a":"limits","b":"rules restricting / a maximum","tr":"sınırlar","fa":"محدودیت‌ها"},{"a":"some","b":"a few / not all","tr":"bazı","fa":"بعضی"},{"a":"may","b":"appears to / suggests","tr":"olabilir","fa":"ممکن است"}],"traps":[{"en":"The text says what people did; a statement about what they preferred, felt or paid is NOT GIVEN unless the text says it too.","tr":"Metin insanların ne yaptığını söyler; neyi tercih ettiklerini, ne hissettiklerini ya da ne ödediklerini söyleyen bir ifade, metin bunu da söylemiyorsa NOT GIVEN’dır.","fa":"متن می‌گوید آدم‌ها چه کردند؛ جمله‌ای درباره‌ی اینکه چه چیزی را ترجیح دادند، چه حسی داشتند یا چقدر پول دادند NOT GIVEN است، مگر اینکه متن آن را هم بگوید."},{"en":"Hedges change the claim: \"there is little proof that the diet helps\" contradicts \"the diet has been proved to help\".","tr":"Çekinceli ifadeler iddiayı değiştirir: \"diyetin işe yaradığına dair çok az kanıt var\", \"diyetin işe yaradığı kanıtlandı\" ile çelişir.","fa":"قیدهای احتیاط ادعا را عوض می‌کنند: «شواهد کمی هست که این رژیم کمک می‌کند» با «ثابت شده که این رژیم کمک می‌کند» تناقض دارد."},{"en":"Who was a product for? \"Made for farmers\" contradicts \"made for city workers\".","tr":"Ürün kimin içindi? \"Çiftçiler için yapıldı\", \"şehirde çalışanlar için yapıldı\" ile çelişir.","fa":"کالا برای چه کسی بود؟ «برای کشاورزها ساخته شد» با «برای کارمندهای شهری ساخته شد» تناقض دارد."}],"example":{"text":"\"Some early cyclists added extra padding to their saddles.\"","item":"Statement: Early cyclists found padded saddles more comfortable than leather ones.","answer":"NOT GIVEN","why":{"en":"The text says what some cyclists did, not what they found more comfortable.","tr":"Metin bazı bisikletçilerin ne yaptığını söylüyor, neyi daha rahat bulduklarını değil.","fa":"متن می‌گوید بعضی دوچرخه‌سوارها چه کردند، نه اینکه چه چیزی را راحت‌تر می‌دانستند."}}},{"id":"RA-tech-proc","ctx":["RA-tech","RA-history"],"title":{"en":"Inventions, machines and buildings","tr":"İcatlar, makineler ve yapılar","fa":"اختراع‌ها، ماشین‌ها و سازه‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"How an invention, a machine or a building works, and how it was developed. Diagram labels name the parts; flow-charts follow how it works; sentences and short answers test purposes and materials.","tr":"Bir icadın, makinenin ya da yapının nasıl çalıştığı ve nasıl geliştirildiği. Diyagram etiketleri parçaları adlandırır; akış şemaları işleyişi izler; cümleler ve kısa cevaplar amaçları ve malzemeleri sınar.","fa":"اینکه یک اختراع، یک ماشین یا یک سازه چطور کار می‌کند و چطور توسعه یافت. برچسب‌های نمودار اسم قطعه‌ها را می‌خواهند؛ فلوچارت‌ها طرز کار را دنبال می‌کنند؛ جمله‌ها و جواب‌های کوتاه هدف و مواد را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Diagram: warm air leaves through the ___","Flow-chart: water is pumped into the ___","Sentence: The first version was made of ___.","Short answer: Which material replaced wood?"],"words":[{"a":"part","b":"component","tr":"parça","fa":"قطعه"},{"a":"made of","b":"built from / constructed with","tr":"... -den yapılmış","fa":"ساخته‌شده از"},{"a":"purpose","b":"designed to / the aim was","tr":"amaç","fa":"هدف"},{"a":"runs on","b":"is powered by","tr":"... ile çalışır","fa":"با ... کار می‌کند"},{"a":"pass through","b":"flow through / circulate","tr":"içinden geçmek","fa":"عبور کردن از"},{"a":"opening","b":"gap / vent","tr":"açıklık","fa":"دریچه"},{"a":"cool","b":"lower the temperature","tr":"soğutmak","fa":"خنک کردن"},{"a":"heat up","b":"warm","tr":"ısıtmak","fa":"گرم کردن"},{"a":"improve","b":"make better / refine","tr":"geliştirmek","fa":"بهتر کردن"},{"a":"prototype","b":"first model / trial version","tr":"ilk örnek","fa":"نمونه‌ی اولیه"},{"a":"efficient","b":"wastes little energy","tr":"verimli","fa":"کارآمد"},{"a":"lightweight","b":"does not weigh much","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"}],"traps":[{"en":"Diagram labels: the text describes what a part does; the label needs its name.","tr":"Diyagram etiketleri: metin parçanın ne işe yaradığını anlatır; etiket onun adını ister.","fa":"برچسب نمودار: متن کار قطعه را توضیح می‌دهد؛ برچسب اسمش را می‌خواهد."},{"en":"Short answers: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Copy a short noun phrase exactly; do not add words.","tr":"Kısa cevaplar: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. Kısa bir isim öbeğini aynen kopyala; kelime ekleme.","fa":"جواب کوتاه: NO MORE THAN TWO WORDS. یک گروه اسمی کوتاه را دقیقاً کپی کن؛ کلمه اضافه نکن."}],"example":{"text":"A solar oven is a simple box lined with foil. Sunlight passes through a glass lid and is reflected onto a black cooking pot, which absorbs the heat.","item":"Diagram: lid made of ___   (ONE WORD ONLY)","answer":"glass","why":{"en":"\"A glass lid\": the material is glass. Foil lines the box, not the lid.","tr":"\"Cam bir kapak\": malzeme cam. Folyo kapağı değil kutuyu kaplıyor.","fa":"«یک درِ شیشه‌ای»: جنسش شیشه است. فویل داخل جعبه است، نه روی در."}},"track":"academic","general":true,"patterns":["RA-tech","RA-history"],"often":{"pattern":"RA-tech","n":18,"of":120,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 18 of the last 120 passages","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 120 metnin 18’inde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۸ متن از ۱۲۰ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"Statements first, then notes","tr":"Önce ifadeler, sonra notlar","fa":"اول جمله‌ها، بعد یادداشت‌ها"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN. Questions 8-13: complete notes with ONE WORD ONLY from the passage. Both sets follow the passage, and the notes usually cover the later paragraphs.","tr":"Soru 1-7: TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 8-13: notları metinden YALNIZCA BİR KELİMEYLE tamamla. İki grup da metni izler; notlar genelde son paragrafları kapsar.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۳: یادداشت‌ها را فقط با یک کلمه از متن کامل کن. هر دو گروه به ترتیب متن‌اند و یادداشت‌ها معمولاً پاراگراف‌های آخر را پوشش می‌دهند."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Underline the key words in each statement: dates, groups of people, comparisons.","tr":"Her ifadedeki anahtar kelimelerin altını çiz: tarihler, insan grupları, karşılaştırmalar.","fa":"زیر کلمه‌های کلیدی هر جمله خط بکش: تاریخ‌ها، گروه‌های آدم‌ها، مقایسه‌ها."},{"en":"Use the dates to find the right paragraph; the statements come in order.","tr":"Doğru paragrafı bulmak için tarihleri kullan; ifadeler sırayla gelir.","fa":"برای پیدا کردن پاراگراف درست از تاریخ‌ها کمک بگیر؛ جمله‌ها به ترتیب‌اند."},{"en":"Ask: does the text say the same, the opposite, or nothing about this exact point?","tr":"Sor: metin bu noktada aynısını mı, tersini mi söylüyor, yoksa hiçbir şey mi?","fa":"بپرس: متن درباره‌ی همین نکته همان را می‌گوید، برعکسش را، یا هیچ؟"},{"en":"For the notes, copy one word in the passage’s form.","tr":"Notlar için tek kelimeyi metindeki biçimiyle kopyala.","fa":"برای یادداشت‌ها یک کلمه را به همان شکل متن کپی کن."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","tr":"FALSE mı NOT GIVEN mı?","fa":"FALSE یا NOT GIVEN؟"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The answer"],"tr":["Metin","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جواب"]},"rows":[["says the same thing in other words","TRUE"],["says the opposite, or a different fact on the same point","FALSE"],["says nothing about this point","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One statement, step by step","tr":"Bir ifade, adım adım","fa":"یک جمله، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Do the following statements agree with the information given in the passage?","text":"\"The first electric kettles appeared in the 1890s. They were slow, taking about twelve minutes to boil water.\"","item":"Statement: Early electric kettles boiled water quickly.","answer":"FALSE","walk":[{"en":"Find the place: \"The first electric kettles\".","tr":"Yeri bul: \"The first electric kettles\".","fa":"جایش را پیدا کن: «The first electric kettles»."},{"en":"Compare: \"slow, about twelve minutes\" against \"quickly\".","tr":"Karşılaştır: \"yavaş, yaklaşık on iki dakika\" ile \"hızlı\".","fa":"مقایسه کن: «کند، حدود دوازده دقیقه» در برابر «سریع»."},{"en":"The text says the opposite: FALSE.","tr":"Metin tersini söylüyor: FALSE.","fa":"متن برعکسش را می‌گوید: FALSE."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"Text: \"The first smartphones were expensive, and only business users bought them at first.\" Statement: \"The first smartphones were popular with teenagers.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"\"Only business users bought them at first\" contradicts \"popular with teenagers\".","tr":"\"İlk başta yalnızca iş kullanıcıları aldı\", \"gençler arasında popülerdi\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"«اولش فقط کاربرهای کاری آن را می‌خریدند» با «بین نوجوان‌ها محبوب بود» تناقض دارد."}},"remember":{"en":"Match each statement to one sentence; compare who, when and how much before you decide.","tr":"Her ifadeyi tek bir cümleyle eşleştir; karar vermeden önce kim, ne zaman ve ne kadar sorularını karşılaştır.","fa":"هر جمله را با یک جمله‌ی متن جور کن؛ قبل از تصمیم، چه کسی، کی و چقدر را مقایسه کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x09-r1-e","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"Academic Reading Passage 1","title":{"en":"The changing running shoe","tr":"Değişen koşu ayakkabısı","fa":"کفش دو و تغییراتش"},"timed":20,"ctx":["RA-tech"],"intro":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 1-13, which are based on Reading Passage 1 below.","passage":"The changing running shoe\n\nRunning is often described as the simplest of all sports: all you need is a pair of shoes. Yet the shoes themselves have become anything but simple. In the last fifty years, their design has changed more than in the previous century and a half, and the arguments about what runners should wear on their feet have never been louder. Scientists, coaches and manufacturers often disagree, and ordinary runners are left to decide for themselves.\n\nThe first shoes made specially for running appeared in the middle of the nineteenth century. They were made of leather and had short metal spikes fixed to the sole, which gave sprinters a better grip on grass and cinder tracks. For running on roads, most people simply wore ordinary leather boots. Later in the century, factories began producing cheap canvas shoes with rubber soles. These were light and flexible, and because they cost so little they became popular for school sports, but the thin soles offered almost no protection from hard surfaces.\n\nFor much of the twentieth century, running shoes changed only slowly. Uppers became lighter as nylon replaced some of the leather, but soles stayed thin. Marathon runners of the 1950s and 1960s ran in shoes with very little cushioning, and many accepted blisters and sore feet as part of the sport. Some top athletes even made their own adjustments, cutting away parts of the upper or adding a layer of rubber to the heel, and a few small companies built shoes by hand for individual runners.\n\nEverything changed in the 1970s, when running for fitness became a popular pastime in North America and Europe. Millions of people who had never raced took up jogging, and manufacturers saw a huge new market. To make running more comfortable for these amateurs, they introduced thick soles made of light foam, with a raised heel that softened the impact of each stride. The new shoes were advertised as a way of protecting knees and backs, and they sold in enormous numbers. For the first time, running shoes were also worn as everyday fashion items by people who never ran at all, which made them even more profitable.\n\nDuring the 1980s and 1990s, shoes became increasingly technical. Companies added cushioning units filled with air or gel, and developed so-called motion-control shoes, designed to stop the foot from rolling inwards too far when it lands. Many specialist shops began to film customers running on a treadmill and recommend a particular type of shoe for their running style. For many customers, this made buying a pair of shoes feel more like a medical decision than a shopping trip.\n\nHowever, research has not always supported these claims. Studies comparing injury rates among runners wearing different kinds of shoes have found little evidence that extra cushioning or motion control reduces injuries. Some researchers now suggest that the best guide may be the simplest one: runners should choose the shoe that feels most comfortable, since comfort appears to be at least as good a predictor of injury as any measurement of the foot.\n\nThe doubts about heavily cushioned shoes helped to fuel a very different trend in the early 2000s. A growing number of runners began to run barefoot or in minimalist shoes with thin, flexible soles. Supporters argued that these encouraged a more natural running style, landing on the front of the foot rather than the heel. The movement attracted great publicity, but it faded within a decade, partly because many runners who switched too quickly were injured, often with painful problems in the foot and lower leg.\n\nThe most recent change has come from the top of the sport. Since the late 2010s, elite road runners have worn shoes that combine very light, highly springy foam with a stiff plate made of carbon fibre inside the sole. These shoes return more of the runner's energy with each step, and world records over long distances have fallen repeatedly. The improvement was so dramatic that the sport's governing body introduced rules limiting the thickness of soles in competition.\n\nSuch shoes are now widely sold to amateurs, often at high prices, and their long-term effects on ordinary runners are not yet known. They also raise an environmental question. The foams used in modern shoes are difficult to recycle, and hundreds of millions of pairs are thrown away every year. A few companies have started to collect worn-out shoes, grind them up and turn them into surfaces for playgrounds and sports tracks, but this remains a small fraction of the total. The simplest of sports, it seems, has left a surprisingly complicated footprint.","groups":[{"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Do the following statements agree with the information given in Reading Passage 1? In boxes 1-7 on your answer sheet, write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The earliest shoes designed for running were made of leather.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"They were made of leather and had short metal spikes","why":{"en":"The first running shoes \"were made of leather\".","tr":"İlk koşu ayakkabıları \"deriden yapılmıştı\".","fa":"اولین کفش‌های دو «از چرم ساخته شده بودند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Canvas shoes with rubber soles were more expensive than leather running shoes.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"because they cost so little","why":{"en":"Canvas shoes were \"cheap\" and \"cost so little\".","tr":"Kanvas ayakkabılar \"ucuzdu\" ve \"çok az tutuyordu\".","fa":"کفش‌های برزنتی «ارزان» بودند و «خیلی کم قیمت داشتند»."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Hand-made running shoes in the 1950s and 1960s cost more than factory-made ones.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"a few small companies built shoes by hand for individual runners","why":{"en":"Hand-made shoes are mentioned, but the text gives no prices.","tr":"El yapımı ayakkabılardan söz ediliyor ama metin fiyat vermiyor.","fa":"از کفش‌های دست‌دوز حرف زده می‌شود، اما متن قیمتی نمی‌دهد."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"The popularity of jogging in the 1970s created a large new market for shoes.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"manufacturers saw a huge new market","why":{"en":"Millions took up jogging, and manufacturers \"saw a huge new market\".","tr":"Milyonlarca kişi koşuya başladı ve üreticiler \"büyük yeni bir pazar gördü\".","fa":"میلیون‌ها نفر شروع به دویدن کردند و تولیدکننده‌ها «بازار تازه‌ی بزرگی دیدند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Thick foam soles were first developed for professional athletes.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"To make running more comfortable for these amateurs","why":{"en":"They were introduced for \"amateurs\", the new joggers, not for professionals.","tr":"Profesyoneller için değil, \"amatörler\", yani yeni koşucular için çıkarıldı.","fa":"برای «آماتورها»، یعنی دونده‌های تازه‌کار، ساخته شدند، نه حرفه‌ای‌ها."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Most customers found running on a treadmill in a shop useful.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Many specialist shops began to film customers running on a treadmill","why":{"en":"Shops filmed customers, but the text does not say what customers thought of it.","tr":"Mağazalar müşterileri filme aldı ama metin müşterilerin bu konuda ne düşündüğünü söylemiyor.","fa":"مغازه‌ها از مشتری‌ها فیلم می‌گرفتند، اما متن نمی‌گوید مشتری‌ها درباره‌اش چه فکری داشتند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Research has shown that motion-control shoes greatly reduce injuries.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"have found little evidence that extra cushioning or motion control reduces injuries","why":{"en":"Studies found \"little evidence\" that motion control reduces injuries.","tr":"Araştırmalar hareket kontrolünün sakatlıkları azalttığına dair \"çok az kanıt\" buldu.","fa":"پژوهش‌ها «شواهد کمی» پیدا کردند که کنترل حرکت آسیب‌ها را کم کند."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]}]},{"instruction":"Questions 8-13. Complete the notes below. Choose ONE WORD ONLY from the passage for each answer. Write your answers in boxes 8-13 on your answer sheet.","qtype":"note","notesTitle":"Recent developments in running shoes","questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Minimalist shoes · supporters said they led to a more ___ way of running","accept":["natural"],"limit":1,"evidence":"encouraged a more natural running style","why":{"en":"\"Encouraged a more natural running style\" = led to a more natural way of running.","tr":"\"Daha doğal bir koşu stilini teşvik etti\".","fa":"«سبک دویدن طبیعی‌تری را تشویق می‌کرد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Minimalist shoes · many runners who changed too fast were ___","accept":["injured"],"limit":1,"evidence":"who switched too quickly were injured","why":{"en":"\"Switched too quickly\" = changed too fast; they \"were injured\".","tr":"\"Çok hızlı geçenler\" sakatlandı.","fa":"کسانی که «خیلی سریع عوض کردند» آسیب دیدند."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Elite shoes · springy foam combined with a stiff ___ of carbon fibre","accept":["plate"],"limit":1,"evidence":"a stiff plate made of carbon fibre","why":{"en":"\"A stiff plate made of carbon fibre\". One word.","tr":"\"Karbon fiberden sert bir plaka\". Tek kelime.","fa":"«یک صفحه‌ی سفت از الیاف کربن». یک کلمه."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"gap","prompt":"Elite shoes · rules now limit the ___ of soles in races","accept":["thickness"],"limit":1,"evidence":"rules limiting the thickness of soles in competition","why":{"en":"\"Rules limiting the thickness of soles in competition\": races = competition.","tr":"\"Yarışmada taban kalınlığını sınırlayan kurallar\".","fa":"«قانون‌هایی که ضخامت زیره را در مسابقه محدود می‌کنند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The future · the foam in modern shoes is hard to ___","accept":["recycle"],"limit":1,"evidence":"The foams used in modern shoes are difficult to recycle","why":{"en":"\"Difficult to recycle\" = hard to recycle. Copy the verb.","tr":"\"Geri dönüştürülmesi zor\". Fiili kopyala.","fa":"«بازیافتش سخت است». فعل را کپی کن."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":13,"kind":"gap","prompt":"The future · some old shoes are made into ___ for playgrounds","accept":["surfaces"],"limit":1,"evidence":"turn them into surfaces for playgrounds","why":{"en":"\"Turn them into surfaces for playgrounds and sports tracks\". Plural.","tr":"\"Oyun alanları ve pistler için zemine dönüştürmek\". Çoğul.","fa":"«تبدیلشان به کف‌پوش برای زمین بازی و پیست». جمع."},"trap":["TR-plural","TR-limit"]}]}],"id":"c-x09-r1-d","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"\"The trend faded within a decade.\" This means it...","options":["grew very quickly","slowly became less popular","was banned"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"To fade = to become weaker or less popular over time.","tr":"Fade = zamanla zayıflamak, popülerliğini yitirmek.","fa":"fade یعنی کم‌کم ضعیف یا کم‌طرفدار شدن."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":3,"prompt":"Note: \"easy to ___\". The passage says \"simple to repair\". What do you write?","options":["repair","repairing","fix"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Copy the verb from the passage in the same form: repair.","tr":"Fiili metindeki biçimiyle kopyala: repair.","fa":"فعل را به همان شکل متن کپی کن: repair."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"The statements in Questions 1-7 mention dates (1950s, 1970s, 1980s). How do they help you?","options":["They are the answers","They show that the statements are TRUE","They show which paragraph to read"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Dates are anchors: they take you to the right paragraph quickly.","tr":"Tarihler çapadır: seni hızlıca doğru paragrafa götürür.","fa":"تاریخ‌ها لنگرند: سریع تو را به پاراگراف درست می‌برند."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"A few companies now collect old phones.\" Statement: \"Old phones are collected by companies at a profit.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"The text says that some companies collect them, not whether they make money from it.","tr":"Metin bazı şirketlerin topladığını söylüyor, bundan para kazanıp kazanmadıklarını değil.","fa":"متن می‌گوید بعضی شرکت‌ها جمعشان می‌کنند، نه اینکه از این کار سود می‌برند یا نه."}}],"id":"c-x09-r1-x","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r1"},"gt":{"explain":{"title":{"en":"GT Reading Section 1: an FAQ and reviews","tr":"GT Reading Section 1: bir SSS sayfası ve yorumlar","fa":"GT Reading Section 1: پرسش‌های متداول و نظرها"},"objective":{"en":"In this lesson you will learn to decide TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on a page of questions and answers, and to match statements to short reviews.","tr":"Bu derste bir soru-cevap sayfasında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN’a karar vermeyi ve ifadeleri kısa yorumlarla eşleştirmeyi öğreneceksin.","fa":"در این درس یاد می‌گیری درباره‌ی یک صفحه‌ی پرسش و پاسخ بین TRUE، FALSE و NOT GIVEN تصمیم بگیری و جمله‌ها را با نظرهای کوتاه جور کنی."},"stats":[{"label":{"en":"Questions","tr":"Soru","fa":"سؤال"},"value":"14"},{"label":{"en":"Texts","tr":"Metin","fa":"متن"},"value":"2"},{"label":{"en":"Time","tr":"Süre","fa":"زمان"},"value":{"en":"about 20 min","tr":"yaklaşık 20 dk","fa":"حدود ۲۰ دقیقه"}}],"context":{"eyebrow":{"en":"1 The context","tr":"1 Bağlam","fa":"۱ بافت"},"head":{"en":"This exam: an island ferry and rain jackets","tr":"Bu sınav: bir ada feribotu ve yağmurluklar","fa":"این آزمون: کشتی جزیره و بارانی‌ها"},"intro":{"en":"GT Section 1 uses short everyday texts: notices, FAQs, adverts and reviews. An FAQ is organised by question, so the questions themselves are your headings.","tr":"GT Section 1 kısa günlük metinler kullanır: duyurular, SSS sayfaları, ilanlar ve yorumlar. Bir SSS soru soru düzenlenmiştir; yani soruların kendisi başlıklarındır.","fa":"GT Section 1 از متن‌های کوتاه روزمره استفاده می‌کند: اطلاعیه، پرسش‌های متداول، آگهی و نظر. صفحه‌ی پرسش‌های متداول بر اساس سؤال مرتب شده، پس خودِ سؤال‌ها عنوان‌های تو هستند."},"technique":{"en":"2 The technique","tr":"2 Teknik","fa":"۲ تکنیک"},"labels":{"asks":{"en":"What this part is about","tr":"Bu kısım ne hakkında","fa":"این بخش درباره‌ی چیست"},"fields":{"en":"Headings you will see","tr":"Göreceğin başlıklar","fa":"عنوان‌هایی که می‌بینی"},"words":{"en":"Words that carry the answers","tr":"Cevabı taşıyan kelimeler","fa":"کلمه‌هایی که جواب را می‌آورند"},"a":{"en":"On the paper","tr":"Kâğıtta","fa":"روی برگه"},"b":{"en":"What you hear or read","tr":"Duyduğun ya da okuduğun","fa":"چیزی که می‌شنوی یا می‌خوانی"},"traps":{"en":"Traps","tr":"Tuzaklar","fa":"دام‌ها"},"example":{"en":"Example","tr":"Örnek","fa":"نمونه"},"ideas":{"en":"Ideas","tr":"Fikirler","fa":"ایده‌ها"}},"cards":[{"id":"x09-r1gt-ctx","exam":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices","GT1-reviews","PARA-rules"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}},"title":{"en":"A transport FAQ and product reviews","tr":"Bir ulaşım SSS sayfası ve ürün yorumları","fa":"پرسش‌های متداول یک شرکت حمل‌ونقل و نظرهای مشتری‌ها"},"asks":{"en":"First, a list of questions and answers from a transport company: timetables, tickets, changes, bikes, bad weather, pets. Then five short reviews of one kind of product, lettered A-E.","tr":"Önce bir ulaşım şirketinin soru-cevap listesi: tarifeler, biletler, değişiklikler, bisikletler, kötü hava, evcil hayvanlar. Sonra aynı türden bir ürün hakkında A-E harfli beş kısa yorum.","fa":"اول فهرستی از پرسش و پاسخ‌های یک شرکت حمل‌ونقل: برنامه‌ی حرکت، بلیت، تغییر، دوچرخه، هوای بد، حیوان خانگی. بعد پنج نظر کوتاه درباره‌ی یک نوع کالا با حرف‌های A تا E."},"fields":["Timetable","Booking","Prices and discounts","Changes and refunds","Bicycles and pets","Size and fit","Waterproof","Comfort"],"words":[{"a":"reduced","b":"fewer / cut back","tr":"azaltılmış","fa":"کم‌شده"},{"a":"in advance","b":"before the day / beforehand","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"free","b":"no charge / carried free","tr":"ücretsiz","fa":"رایگان"},{"a":"half price","b":"pay 50%","tr":"yarı fiyatına","fa":"نصف قیمت"},{"a":"a discount","b":"reduced fares / money off","tr":"indirim","fa":"تخفیف"},{"a":"refund","b":"money back","tr":"para iadesi","fa":"پس دادن پول"},{"a":"valid","b":"can be used / accepted","tr":"geçerli","fa":"معتبر"},{"a":"cancelled","b":"not running / called off","tr":"iptal edilmiş","fa":"لغوشده"},{"a":"on a lead","b":"held on a rope or strap","tr":"tasmalı","fa":"با قلاده"},{"a":"a bigger size","b":"send it back and order a large","tr":"bir beden büyük","fa":"سایز بزرگ‌تر"},{"a":"lets water in","b":"water started coming through","tr":"su alıyor","fa":"آب پس می‌دهد"},{"a":"smart","b":"fine for work / looks good","tr":"şık","fa":"شیک"}],"traps":[{"en":"A rule has an exception: \"Dogs must stay outside... Assistance dogs may travel in all areas.\" Check which group the statement is about.","tr":"Bir kuralın istisnası vardır: \"Köpekler dışarıda kalmalı... Yardımcı köpekler her yere girebilir.\" İfadenin hangi grupla ilgili olduğuna bak.","fa":"یک قانون استثنا دارد: «سگ‌ها باید بیرون بمانند... سگ‌های راهنما همه‌جا می‌روند». ببین جمله درباره‌ی کدام گروه است."},{"en":"Reduced is not free: \"reduced fares\" contradicts \"travel free\".","tr":"İndirimli ücretsiz değildir: \"indirimli bilet\", \"ücretsiz seyahat\" ile çelişir.","fa":"تخفیف یعنی رایگان نیست: «بلیت با تخفیف» با «سفر رایگان» تناقض دارد."},{"en":"A review may mention running, helmets or rain without matching the statement. Check every part.","tr":"Bir yorum koşudan, kasktan ya da yağmurdan söz edip yine de ifadeye uymayabilir. Her parçayı kontrol et.","fa":"ممکن است یک نظر از دویدن، کلاه ایمنی یا باران حرف بزند و باز هم با جمله جور نباشد. همه‌ی بخش‌ها را چک کن."}],"example":{"text":"FAQ: \"Bicycles are carried free, but space is limited to ten per train.\"","item":"Statement: Passengers must pay to take a bicycle on the train.","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"\"Carried free\" contradicts \"must pay\". The limit on space is a different point.","tr":"\"Ücretsiz taşınır\", \"ödemek zorunda\" ile çelişiyor. Yer sınırı ayrı bir nokta.","fa":"«رایگان حمل می‌شود» با «باید پول بدهند» تناقض دارد. محدودیت جا نکته‌ی دیگری است."}}},{"id":"GT1-notices","ctx":["GT1-notices"],"title":{"en":"Notices, rules and FAQs","tr":"Duyurular, kurallar ve SSS","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول"},"asks":{"en":"Notices, rules and frequently asked questions for a service: a tram, a leisure centre, a block of flats, a competition. Questions test rules, conditions, dates and exceptions.","tr":"Bir hizmet için duyurular, kurallar ve sık sorulan sorular: tramvay, spor merkezi, apartman, yarışma. Sorular kuralları, koşulları, tarihleri ve istisnaları sınar.","fa":"اطلاعیه، قانون و پرسش‌های متداول برای یک خدمت: تراموا، مرکز ورزشی، یک ساختمان مسکونی، یک مسابقه. سؤال‌ها قانون‌ها، شرط‌ها، تاریخ‌ها و استثناها را می‌سنجند."},"fields":["Passengers must buy a ticket before boarding.","Children under five travel free.","Refunds are given for delays of over 30 minutes.","Residents may leave bicycles in the hallway."],"words":[{"a":"must","b":"are required to","tr":"zorunda","fa":"باید"},{"a":"not allowed","b":"prohibited / not permitted","tr":"yasak","fa":"ممنوع"},{"a":"within 14 days","b":"in less than two weeks","tr":"14 gün içinde","fa":"ظرف ۱۴ روز"},{"a":"can claim","b":"are entitled to / are eligible for","tr":"talep edebilir","fa":"می‌تواند درخواست کند"},{"a":"apply","b":"submit a form","tr":"başvurmak","fa":"درخواست دادن"},{"a":"proof","b":"a receipt / evidence of","tr":"kanıt","fa":"مدرک"},{"a":"residents","b":"people living in the building","tr":"sakinler","fa":"ساکنان"},{"a":"compensation","b":"money for a problem you had","tr":"tazminat","fa":"غرامت"},{"a":"beforehand","b":"in advance","tr":"önceden","fa":"از قبل"},{"a":"except","b":"apart from / with the exception of","tr":"hariç","fa":"به‌جز"},{"a":"responsible for","b":"must take care of","tr":"... -den sorumlu","fa":"مسئولِ"},{"a":"on request","b":"if you ask","tr":"talep üzerine","fa":"در صورت درخواست"}],"traps":[{"en":"Exceptions: \"all passengers must..., except season-ticket holders\". A statement about everyone may be FALSE.","tr":"İstisnalar: \"bütün yolcular ... zorunda, abonman sahipleri hariç\". Herkes hakkındaki bir ifade FALSE olabilir.","fa":"استثناها: «همه‌ی مسافران باید...، به‌جز دارندگان بلیت فصلی». جمله‌ای درباره‌ی همه ممکن است FALSE باشد."},{"en":"Numbers in conditions: \"30 minutes or more\" and \"over 30 minutes\" are not the same.","tr":"Koşullardaki sayılar: \"30 dakika veya daha fazla\" ile \"30 dakikadan fazla\" aynı değildir.","fa":"عددها در شرط‌ها: «۳۰ دقیقه یا بیشتر» با «بیش از ۳۰ دقیقه» یکی نیست."}],"example":{"text":"Delay Repay: if your train arrives 30 minutes or more late, you can claim 50% of your ticket price. Claims must be made within 28 days of travel.","item":"Statement: Passengers can claim the full price of their ticket.  (TRUE / FALSE / NOT GIVEN)","answer":"FALSE","why":{"en":"The notice says 50%, which contradicts \"the full price\".","tr":"Duyuru %50 diyor; bu \"tam fiyat\" ile çelişiyor.","fa":"اطلاعیه می‌گوید ۵۰٪، که با «قیمت کامل» در تضاد است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-notices"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-notices","n":22,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 22 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 22’sinde","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۲۲ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}},{"id":"GT1-reviews","ctx":["GT1-reviews"],"title":{"en":"Product and service reviews","tr":"Ürün ve hizmet değerlendirmeleri","fa":"نقد و معرفی کالا و خدمات"},"asks":{"en":"Short reviews or descriptions A-F of products or places: sleeping bags, kitchen machines, cafes, hotels, phone apps. Questions ask which one has a feature, or which review says something.","tr":"Ürünler ya da yerler hakkında A-F harfli kısa değerlendirmeler veya tanıtımlar: uyku tulumları, mutfak aletleri, kafeler, oteller, telefon uygulamaları. Sorular hangisinin bir özelliği olduğunu ya da hangi yorumun bir şey söylediğini sorar.","fa":"نقدها یا معرفی‌های کوتاه A تا F درباره‌ی کالاها یا مکان‌ها: کیسه‌خواب، وسایل آشپزخانه، کافه، هتل، اپلیکیشن. سؤال‌ها می‌پرسند کدام یک ویژگی را دارد، یا کدام نقد چیزی را می‌گوید."},"fields":["Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","Which cafe has outdoor seating?","Which app works without the internet?","Which hotel is suitable for families?"],"words":[{"a":"lightweight","b":"weighs very little / easy to carry","tr":"hafif","fa":"سبک"},{"a":"durable","b":"lasts for years / hard-wearing","tr":"dayanıklı","fa":"بادوام"},{"a":"value for money","b":"a good price for what you get","tr":"fiyatına değer","fa":"به‌صرفه"},{"a":"noisy","b":"loud","tr":"gürültülü","fa":"پرسروصدا"},{"a":"spacious","b":"lots of room","tr":"ferah","fa":"جادار"},{"a":"easy to clean","b":"wipes clean","tr":"kolay temizlenir","fa":"راحت تمیز می‌شود"},{"a":"offline","b":"without an internet connection","tr":"çevrimdışı","fa":"آفلاین"},{"a":"outdoor seating","b":"tables outside","tr":"dışarıda oturma yeri","fa":"میز در فضای باز"},{"a":"guarantee","b":"free repairs for two years","tr":"garanti","fa":"گارانتی"},{"a":"compact","b":"small / takes up little space","tr":"küçük, kompakt","fa":"جمع‌وجور"},{"a":"fully booked","b":"no rooms left","tr":"tamamen dolu","fa":"کاملاً پر"},{"a":"suitable for families","b":"children welcome / cots available","tr":"ailelere uygun","fa":"مناسب خانواده"}],"traps":[{"en":"Superlatives: \"the lightest\" needs a comparison with all the others, not just the word \"light\".","tr":"Üstünlük sıfatları: \"en hafif\" diğerlerinin hepsiyle karşılaştırma ister, yalnızca \"hafif\" kelimesi yetmez.","fa":"صفت عالی: «سبک‌ترین» یعنی مقایسه با همه‌ی بقیه، نه فقط کلمه‌ی «سبک»."},{"en":"A review may mention a feature only to say that it is missing.","tr":"Bir yorum bir özellikten yalnızca eksik olduğunu söylemek için bahsedebilir.","fa":"یک نقد ممکن است به ویژگی‌ای فقط اشاره کند تا بگوید ندارد."}],"example":{"text":"A  The Trekker 200 weighs 900 g and packs down small.\nB  The Summit weighs just 650 g, though it is not quite as warm.\nC  The Polar Pro is the warmest of the three, at 1.4 kg.","item":"Which sleeping bag is the lightest?","answer":"B","why":{"en":"Compare all three: 650 g is less than 900 g and 1.4 kg.","tr":"Üçünü de karşılaştır: 650 g, 900 g ve 1,4 kg’dan az.","fa":"هر سه را مقایسه کن: ۶۵۰ گرم از ۹۰۰ گرم و ۱٫۴ کیلو کمتر است."}},"track":"gt","general":true,"patterns":["GT1-reviews"],"often":{"pattern":"GT1-reviews","n":19,"of":65,"label":{"en":"Comes up often in the real exam: 19 of the last 65 texts","tr":"Gerçek sınavda sık çıkar: son 65 metnin 19’unda","fa":"در آزمون واقعی زیاد می‌آید: در ۱۹ متن از ۶۵ متنِ اخیر"}}}]},"points":[{"eyebrow":{"en":"In the exam","tr":"Sınavda","fa":"در آزمون"},"head":{"en":"An FAQ, then five reviews","tr":"Bir SSS, sonra beş yorum","fa":"یک صفحه‌ی پرسش‌ها، بعد پنج نظر"},"body":{"en":"Questions 1-7: TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN on the FAQ. Questions 8-14: write the letter of the review, A-E; letters can be used more than once. Aim for about 20 minutes.","tr":"Soru 1-7: SSS hakkında TRUE, FALSE ya da NOT GIVEN. Soru 8-14: yorumun harfini (A-E) yaz; harfler birden fazla kullanılabilir. Yaklaşık 20 dakika hedefle.","fa":"سؤال‌های ۱ تا ۷: TRUE، FALSE یا NOT GIVEN درباره‌ی صفحه‌ی پرسش‌ها. سؤال‌های ۸ تا ۱۴: حرف نظر (A تا E) را بنویس؛ حرف‌ها را می‌شود بیش از یک بار به کار برد. حدود ۲۰ دقیقه وقت بگذار."}},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The method","tr":"Yöntem","fa":"روش"},"head":{"en":"Four steps","tr":"Dört adım","fa":"چهار قدم"},"steps":[{"en":"Match each statement to the FAQ question it belongs to: bikes, dogs, refunds.","tr":"Her ifadeyi ait olduğu SSS sorusuyla eşleştir: bisikletler, köpekler, iadeler.","fa":"هر جمله را با سؤالِ مربوطش در صفحه جور کن: دوچرخه، سگ، بازپرداخت."},{"en":"Check the exact group and condition: residents, students, before 24 hours.","tr":"Tam grubu ve koşulu kontrol et: adada yaşayanlar, öğrenciler, 24 saatten önce.","fa":"گروه و شرط دقیق را چک کن: ساکنان جزیره، دانشجوها، پیش از ۲۴ ساعت."},{"en":"For the reviews, read all five quickly and note one strong point and one weak point for each.","tr":"Yorumlar için beşini de hızla oku ve her biri için bir güçlü, bir zayıf yan not et.","fa":"برای نظرها هر پنج تا را سریع بخوان و برای هرکدام یک نقطه‌ی قوت و یک ضعف یادداشت کن."},{"en":"Match the whole statement, not one word: \"a helmet\" may appear in two reviews.","tr":"Tek kelimeyi değil, ifadenin tamamını eşleştir: \"kask\" iki yorumda geçebilir.","fa":"کل جمله را جور کن، نه یک کلمه را: «کلاه ایمنی» ممکن است در دو نظر بیاید."}]},{"eyebrow":{"en":"The trap","tr":"Tuzak","fa":"دام"},"head":{"en":"Rules and exceptions","tr":"Kurallar ve istisnalar","fa":"قانون‌ها و استثناها"},"table":{"headers":{"en":["The text","The statement","Answer"],"tr":["Metin","İfade","Cevap"],"fa":["متن","جمله","جواب"]},"rows":[["reduced fares all year","residents travel free","FALSE"],["dogs on the outside deck; assistance dogs anywhere","pet dogs may sit in the café","FALSE"],["students pay half price","students must show a card on board","NOT GIVEN"]]}}],"example":{"eyebrow":{"en":"Worked example","tr":"Çözümlü örnek","fa":"مثال حل‌شده"},"head":{"en":"One review match, step by step","tr":"Bir yorum eşleştirmesi, adım adım","fa":"جور کردن یک نظر، قدم به قدم"},"instruction":"Which review mentions the following?","text":"A \"Light and warm, but the zip broke after a month.\" B \"Heavy, but I wore it every day for three winters and it still looks new.\"","item":"Statement: It has lasted a long time.","answer":"B","walk":[{"en":"The idea is long life: \"lasted a long time\".","tr":"Fikir uzun ömür: \"uzun süre dayandı\".","fa":"ایده دوام طولانی است: «مدت زیادی دوام آورده»."},{"en":"A broke after a month: the opposite.","tr":"A bir ay sonra bozuldu: tam tersi.","fa":"A بعد از یک ماه خراب شد: برعکسش."},{"en":"B: \"three winters... still looks new\" = it has lasted.","tr":"B: \"üç kış... hâlâ yeni gibi\" = uzun süre dayandı.","fa":"B: «سه زمستان... هنوز نو به نظر می‌رسد» یعنی دوام آورده."}]},"quick":{"prompt":"FAQ: \"Tickets can be changed up to two hours before departure.\" Statement: \"Tickets can be changed on the day of travel.\" TRUE, FALSE or NOT GIVEN?","options":["TRUE","FALSE","NOT GIVEN"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"Up to two hours before departure includes the day of travel, so TRUE.","tr":"Kalkıştan iki saat öncesine kadar, seyahat gününü de kapsar; yani TRUE.","fa":"تا دو ساعت پیش از حرکت شامل روز سفر هم می‌شود، پس TRUE."}},"remember":{"en":"Find the right question in the FAQ, check the group and the condition, and match whole ideas in the reviews.","tr":"SSS’de doğru soruyu bul, grubu ve koşulu kontrol et, yorumlarda fikirlerin tamamını eşleştir.","fa":"در صفحه‌ی پرسش‌ها سؤال درست را پیدا کن، گروه و شرط را چک کن و در نظرها کل ایده‌ها را جور کن."},"type":"explain","id":"c-x09-r1-e-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r1"},"drill":{"type":"drill","skill":"reading","part":"General Training Reading Section 1","title":{"en":"An island ferry and rain jackets","tr":"Bir ada feribotu ve yağmurluklar","fa":"کشتی جزیره و بارانی‌ها"},"timed":20,"ctx":["GT1-notices","GT1-reviews"],"texts":[{"title":"Northsound Island Ferries: frequently asked questions","kind":"FAQ","body":"How often do the ferries run?\nFrom April to October there are six crossings a day in each direction, the first leaving the mainland at 7.15 am. From November to March the service is reduced to four crossings a day. The crossing takes about 50 minutes, depending on the weather.\n\nDo I need to book?\nFoot passengers can simply buy a ticket at the terminal or on board. If you are taking a car, you must book in advance, as space on the car deck is limited. In July and August, car spaces are often fully booked several weeks ahead.\n\nHow much does it cost?\nA return ticket for an adult foot passenger costs £14. Children under five travel free, and children aged five to fifteen pay half price. Island residents receive a discount card, which gives them reduced fares all year.\n\nCan I change my booking?\nCar bookings can be changed free of charge up to 24 hours before departure. After that, a fee of £10 is charged. Foot passenger tickets cannot be refunded, but they are valid on any crossing on the date shown.\n\nCan I take my bicycle?\nYes. Bicycles are carried free on all crossings, but there is room for only twelve on each boat, so please arrive early in summer.\n\nWhat happens if the weather is bad?\nIn strong winds, crossings may be delayed or cancelled. We post updates on our website and send text messages to everyone who has booked. If your crossing is cancelled, you can travel on the next available boat or claim a full refund.\n\nAre there facilities on board?\nAll our ferries have a café serving hot drinks and snacks, and there are toilets on every deck. The larger ferry, which operates in summer, also has a children's play area.\n\nCan I bring my dog?\nDogs are welcome, but they must stay on a lead and remain on the outside deck or in the pet area. Assistance dogs may travel in all passenger areas."},{"title":"Rain jackets: customer reviews","kind":"reviews","body":"A  Brightwater Shell\nI wore this on a four-day walk in heavy rain and stayed completely dry. It folds into its own pocket, which is handy when the sun comes out again. The only downside is the sizing: I usually wear a medium, but I had to send it back and order a large.\n\nB  Fellside Classic\nA heavy, old-fashioned jacket that keeps out wind as well as rain. It is perfect for winter, but far too warm for anything energetic in summer. It was expensive, though it came with a ten-year repair service, which I have already used once for a broken zip. The repair was done within a week, and I paid nothing.\n\nC  Tern Packable\nVery cheap, and you get what you pay for. It kept me dry for about an hour, then water started coming through at the shoulders. Fine for a quick walk to the shops, but not for a day in the hills. I have now bought something better and keep this one in the car for emergencies.\n\nD  Harbour Coat\nSmart enough to wear to work, so I use it every day for my walk to the station. It is longer than most jackets, so my legs stay dry too. The hood is a bit small, and it doesn't fit well over a cycling helmet. Several colleagues have asked where I bought it, which says a lot.\n\nE  Skerry Light\nI bought this for running and it is excellent: so light that I hardly notice it, and it doesn't make me sweat. The bright colour also means drivers can see me easily in the dark. My one complaint is that it has no pockets at all, so I have to carry my keys and phone in a separate belt."}],"groups":[{"text":0,"instruction":"Questions 1-7. Do the following statements agree with the information given in the text? Write TRUE if the statement agrees with the information, FALSE if the statement contradicts the information, NOT GIVEN if there is no information on this.","qtype":"tfng","questions":[{"n":1,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"There are fewer crossings in winter than in summer.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"From November to March the service is reduced to four crossings a day","why":{"en":"Six a day in summer, \"reduced to four\" in winter.","tr":"Yazın günde altı, kışın \"dörde düşürülüyor\".","fa":"تابستان روزی شش سفر و زمستان «به چهار کاهش می‌یابد»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":2,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Foot passengers have to book before they travel.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"Foot passengers can simply buy a ticket at the terminal or on board","why":{"en":"They can buy a ticket at the terminal or on board, so booking is not required.","tr":"Bileti terminalde ya da gemide alabilirler; yani rezervasyon şart değil.","fa":"می‌توانند بلیت را در ترمینال یا روی کشتی بخرند، پس رزرو لازم نیست."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF"]},{"n":3,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Children under five must sit with an adult during the crossing.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Children under five travel free","why":{"en":"The text says they travel free; it says nothing about where they sit.","tr":"Metin ücretsiz seyahat ettiklerini söylüyor; nerede oturacaklarından söz etmiyor.","fa":"متن می‌گوید رایگان سفر می‌کنند؛ درباره‌ی جای نشستنشان چیزی نمی‌گوید."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-samewords"]},{"n":4,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Island residents travel free during the winter.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"which gives them reduced fares all year","why":{"en":"Residents get \"reduced fares all year\", not free travel.","tr":"Adada yaşayanlar \"yıl boyu indirimli bilet\" alıyor, ücretsiz değil.","fa":"ساکنان جزیره «تمام سال بلیت با تخفیف» می‌گیرند، نه سفر رایگان."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":5,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Car bookings can only be changed online.","correct":"NOT GIVEN","evidence":"Car bookings can be changed free of charge up to 24 hours before departure","why":{"en":"The text gives the time limit and the fee, but not how the change is made.","tr":"Metin süre sınırını ve ücreti veriyor ama değişikliğin nasıl yapılacağını söylemiyor.","fa":"متن مهلت و هزینه را می‌گوید، اما نه اینکه تغییر چطور انجام می‌شود."},"trap":["TR-NGvsF","TR-hedge"]},{"n":6,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Passengers who have booked are told about cancellations by text message.","correct":"TRUE","evidence":"send text messages to everyone who has booked","why":{"en":"\"We... send text messages to everyone who has booked.\"","tr":"\"Rezervasyon yapan herkese kısa mesaj gönderiyoruz.\"","fa":"«به همه‌ی کسانی که رزرو کرده‌اند پیامک می‌فرستیم»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":7,"kind":"tfng","prompt":"Pet dogs are allowed to sit with their owners in the café.","correct":"FALSE","evidence":"remain on the outside deck or in the pet area","why":{"en":"Dogs must stay on the outside deck or in the pet area; only assistance dogs go everywhere.","tr":"Köpekler dış güvertede ya da evcil hayvan bölümünde kalmalı; her yere yalnızca yardımcı köpekler girebilir.","fa":"سگ‌ها باید روی عرشه‌ی بیرونی یا قسمت حیوانات بمانند؛ فقط سگ‌های راهنما همه‌جا می‌روند."},"trap":["TR-detail"]}]},{"text":1,"instruction":"Questions 8-14. Look at the five reviews of rain jackets, A-E. For which jacket are the following statements true? Write the correct letter, A-E, in boxes 8-14 on your answer sheet. NB You may use any letter more than once.","qtype":"match-info","bank":["A","B","C","D","E"],"questions":[{"n":8,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is too warm for active use in summer.","correct":1,"evidence":"far too warm for anything energetic in summer","why":{"en":"B: \"far too warm for anything energetic in summer\".","tr":"B: \"yazın hareketli bir şey için fazla sıcak\".","fa":"B: «برای هر کار پرتحرکی در تابستان خیلی گرم است»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":9,"kind":"match","prompt":"The buyer had to exchange it for a bigger size.","correct":0,"evidence":"I had to send it back and order a large","why":{"en":"A: \"send it back and order a large\".","tr":"A: \"geri gönderip large sipariş etmek zorunda kaldım\".","fa":"A: «مجبور شدم پسش بفرستم و سایز لارج سفارش بدهم»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":10,"kind":"match","prompt":"It stopped keeping the rain out after a short time.","correct":2,"evidence":"It kept me dry for about an hour","why":{"en":"C: dry \"for about an hour\", then water came through.","tr":"C: \"yaklaşık bir saat\" kuru tuttu, sonra su geçti.","fa":"C: «حدود یک ساعت» خشک نگه داشت و بعد آب رد شد."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":11,"kind":"match","prompt":"It makes the wearer easy to see at night.","correct":4,"evidence":"drivers can see me easily in the dark","why":{"en":"E: the bright colour means \"drivers can see me easily in the dark\".","tr":"E: parlak renk sayesinde \"sürücüler beni karanlıkta kolayca görebiliyor\".","fa":"E: رنگ روشنش باعث می‌شود «راننده‌ها در تاریکی راحت مرا ببینند»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":12,"kind":"match","prompt":"It looks suitable for the workplace.","correct":3,"evidence":"Smart enough to wear to work","why":{"en":"D: \"smart enough to wear to work\".","tr":"D: \"işe giyecek kadar şık\".","fa":"D: «آن‌قدر شیک که سر کار هم می‌شود پوشید»."},"trap":["TR-detail"]},{"n":13,"kind":"match","prompt":"The company fixed it without charging the customer.","correct":1,"evidence":"The repair was done within a week, and I paid nothing","why":{"en":"B again: the repair service fixed the zip and \"I paid nothing\".","tr":"Yine B: tamir servisi fermuarı onardı ve \"hiçbir şey ödemedim\".","fa":"باز هم B: سرویس تعمیر زیپ را درست کرد و «هیچ پولی ندادم»."},"trap":["TR-paraphrase"]},{"n":14,"kind":"match","prompt":"It is difficult to wear with a helmet.","correct":3,"evidence":"doesn't fit well over a cycling helmet","why":{"en":"D: the hood \"doesn’t fit well over a cycling helmet\". E is used for running, but no helmet is mentioned.","tr":"D: kapüşon \"bisiklet kaskının üstüne iyi oturmuyor\". E koşu için kullanılıyor ama kasktan söz yok.","fa":"D: کلاهش «روی کلاه دوچرخه‌سواری خوب جا نمی‌شود». E برای دویدن است، اما حرفی از کلاه ایمنی نیست."},"trap":["TR-samewords"]}]}],"id":"c-x09-r1-d-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r1"},"exit":{"type":"exit","items":[{"tests":"word","point":1,"prompt":"An FAQ says tickets are \"valid on any crossing on the date shown\". Valid means...","options":["must be shown","are free","can be used"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Valid = accepted, able to be used.","tr":"Valid = geçerli, kullanılabilir.","fa":"valid یعنی معتبر، قابل استفاده."}},{"tests":"paraphrase","point":1,"prompt":"A statement says \"you get your money back\". Which words in an FAQ mean the same?","options":["pay a small fee","claim a full refund","change your booking"],"correct":1,"why":{"en":"A refund = money returned to you.","tr":"Refund = sana geri verilen para.","fa":"refund یعنی پولی که به تو برمی‌گردانند."}},{"tests":"method","point":2,"prompt":"A statement is about bicycles. Where in an FAQ do you look first?","options":["under the question about bicycles","at the first answer","at the last answer"],"correct":0,"why":{"en":"In an FAQ, each question is a heading: go straight to the matching one.","tr":"Bir SSS’de her soru bir başlıktır: doğrudan ilgili olana git.","fa":"در صفحه‌ی پرسش‌ها هر سؤال یک عنوان است: مستقیم برو سراغ همان."}},{"tests":"trap","point":3,"prompt":"Text: \"Students pay half price.\" Statement: \"Students travel free.\"","options":["TRUE","NOT GIVEN","FALSE"],"correct":2,"why":{"en":"Half price is not free: the text contradicts the statement.","tr":"Yarı fiyat ücretsiz değildir: metin ifadeyle çelişiyor.","fa":"نصف قیمت یعنی رایگان نیست: متن با جمله تناقض دارد."}}],"id":"c-x09-r1-x-gt","course":"ielts-exams","exam":"exam-09","unit":"x09-r1"}}}; })(globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS = globalThis.IELTS_EXAMS || {});
